{"description":"The rest of the ADR-035 envelope has the same gap provenance had: `toUnit` does not project `sourcePromptHash`, `confidence`, `sourceCommitSha` or `captureMeta`, and `buildFrontmatter`/`buildJSONAuthoring` render none of them. `validUntil` and `lastConfirmed` are projected into the unit but not rendered back into the artifact, so the freshness horizon declared by an artifact also fails to survive export -\u003e import -\u003e export.","impact":"Freshness is the one with teeth: a validity horizon that disappears on transport means an imported repository silently loses the date saying when its knowledge must be re-confirmed, and the freshness projection then reports the artifact as never expiring. The capture fields matter less individually but the same way — they are claims about how knowledge was obtained, and losing them resets it to the human default with no finding.","acceptanceCriteria":"- Every field in the ADR-035 envelope survives export -\u003e import -\u003e export for both the Markdown and the JSON adapter, or the omitted ones are documented in the exchange spec as transport-only.\n- A round-trip test covers a unit with `validUntil` and `lastConfirmed` set."}